NAME
       timeout - run a command with a time limit

SYNOPSIS
       timeout [-s SIGNAL] DURATION COMMAND [ARGUMENT]...

DESCRIPTION
       timeout starts COMMAND and stops it if it is still running after
       DURATION (seconds, or a number with s, m, h or d). It exits with the
       command's own status, or with 124 when the time ran out. Scripts use
       it so that a command that hangs (a network test, for example) cannot
       block them forever.

OPTIONS
       -s, --signal=SIGNAL
              The signal sent when the time is up (TERM by default).

EXAMPLES
           timeout 5 curl -s http://server2/

SEE ALSO
       sleep(1), kill(1)
